  "source": {
    "title": "Ballymena Urban District Council minute book, January 1920 - March 1925, pp. 1-2: \"Election of Urban District Councillors, Ballymena, 15th January 1920. Result of Poll\" (PRONI LA/14/2/CA/4; Keep note \"LA/14/2/CA/4\", photos #7 and #8, counting from 0)",
    "publisher": "Public Record Office of Northern Ireland (Ballymena Borough Council records)",
    "kind": "official",
    "check": "every count read from the photographed count sheet: the first preferences add to the valid vote written on the sheet, every transfer column adds to the amount transferred, and each count adds to the valid vote with the non-transferable papers; names as the sheet writes them (the unsuccessful candidates by surname only); no party labels"
  },
  "partyLabels": "none-recorded",
  "note": "Proportional representation (single transferable vote) under the Local Government (Ireland) Act 1919; polled 15 January 1920. Ballymena Urban District had three wards of five members each from 1905 (Local Government Board Order No. 1/1904). 854 valid votes; quota 143. The ward returned 5 members, elected in the order Lamont, Morrow, Wilson, Craig, McIlhagga; McIlhagga was elected on 131 votes, below the quota. The elected members' full names are from the sheet's \"elected\" column; it gives the unsuccessful candidates' surnames only."
}
